We output the calendar event data in a structured format.
There are two ways to output the data:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Just the events.
\item For each event, we output one line per booked student.
  And one line for any free slots.
\end{enumerate}
We'll add an option to choose between these two modes.
<<add calendar list arguments>>=
calendar_list_parser.add_argument("--bookings", "-b",
  action="store_true", default=False,
  help="Output one line per booked student and one line for free slots "
       "(only for appointment group events)")
@

Canvas uses [[child_events]] in two different ways.  For an ordinary
calendar event it may contain section-level child events, while for an
appointment group it contains booking-related child events.  Only the
appointment-group case carries booking metadata such as
[[available_slots]] and [[participants_per_appointment]], so we check for
those fields before we format booking output.
<<functions>>=
def get_appointment_booking_data(event):
  """Return appointment-group booking data for ``event`` or ``None``."""
  available_slots = getattr(event, 'available_slots', None)
  participants_per_appointment = getattr(
    event, 'participants_per_appointment', None)
  appointment_group_id = getattr(event, 'appointment_group_id', None)
  child_events = getattr(event, 'child_events', None)

  if all(value is None for value in (
      appointment_group_id,
      participants_per_appointment,
      available_slots,
  )):
    return None

  return {
    'available_slots': available_slots,
    'participants_per_appointment': participants_per_appointment,
    'child_events': child_events or [],
  }
@

